# ADR-004: Testing Strategy

## Status

Accepted

## Context

{{.ServiceName}} needs a consistent testing approach that verifies business logic independently from infrastructure.

## Decision
{{- if .HasUnitTests}}

### Unit Tests
- Table-driven tests with `t.Run()` sub-tests for all service and domain logic
- Mock outbound ports via interfaces — never depend on concrete adapters in unit tests
- Test files co-located with source: `foo_test.go` next to `foo.go`
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasIntegrationTests}}

### Integration Tests
- Use testcontainers-go to spin up real databases and infrastructure in tests
- Build tag `//go:build integration` to separate from unit tests
- Run with `go test -tags=integration ./...`
{{- end}}
{{- if .HasTestHelpers}}

### Test Helpers
- Shared test utilities in `internal/testutil/`
- All helpers call `t.Helper()` for accurate failure reporting
{{- end}}

## Consequences

- Unit tests run fast and can be executed on every save
{{- if .HasIntegrationTests}}
- Integration tests require Docker but verify real infrastructure behavior
{{- end}}
- Mocking via interfaces ensures tests break when contracts change, not when implementations change

